# Foundry CMS API base URL (no trailing slash). Point it at whichever
# backend this checkout should talk to:
#
#   http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/v1     `php artisan serve --port=8001`
#   http://foundry-cms.test/api/v1   a Valet site
#
# Prefer the port form when running several worktrees: each one talks
# to its own backend, and no proxy or certificate is involved. Run the
# backend with PHP_CLI_SERVER_WORKERS=4 — Astro SSR fans out
# concurrent API calls and a single-worker server serialises them.
FOUNDRY_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/v1

# Optional — preview token forwarded as X-Preview-Token, which makes
# draft websites and pages visible. Must match CMS_PREVIEW_TOKEN in
# the backend's .env (see config/cms.php); when the backend leaves it
# unset, preview is off and only published websites render. Dev and
# staging only — production must never serve drafts.
# FOUNDRY_PREVIEW_TOKEN=

# ─── Serving several worktrees at once ─────────────────────────
# Multi-tenant routing dispatches by the HTTP Host header against
# WebsiteLocale.hostname rows, so the two axes are independent:
#
#   the PORT picks the checkout      ASTRO_PORT below
#   the HOSTNAME picks the website   http://site-b.foundry-astro.test:4322/
#
# Reaching a `.test` hostname on a dev-server port needs no proxy —
# only a resolver mapping `*.test` to 127.0.0.1 (Valet installs one
# via dnsmasq; /etc/hosts entries work too). `localhost:<port>` falls
# back to WEBSITE_BUILD_HOSTNAME below.
#
# Do NOT set HMR_VIA_HTTPS_PROXY in this mode: it pins Vite's
# live-reload to wss://<host>:443, i.e. through the proxy to whichever
# dev server it fronts — usually the wrong worktree.
# ASTRO_PORT=4321

# ─── Build-scope variables ─────────────────────────────────────
# `WEBSITE_BUILD_*` describes which website / locales / paths the
# current build covers. Implicitly all about Foundry; the `WEBSITE_`
# prefix distinguishes them from `FOUNDRY_API_*` (connection config).

# Required at BUILD time: `getStaticPaths` asks the CMS which URLs
# this website serves, and returns nothing without a hostname.
#
# In DEV it names the website that `http://localhost:<port>/` shows —
# no request carries a usable Host there, so the middleware falls back
# to this value (see src/middleware.ts). Browsing by hostname instead
# (`http://site-b.foundry-astro.test:4321/`) ignores it entirely, so
# every website stays reachable whatever this is set to.
#
# When set at build time, this hostname also scopes the build output:
# artefacts go to `dist/<hostname>/{client,server}/` instead of plain
# `dist/`. Lets multiple sites coexist locally — serve each with
# `npm run preview:static <hostname> [--port 4323]`.
WEBSITE_BUILD_HOSTNAME=site-a.foundry-astro.test

# Optional locale filter — comma-separated locale codes. When set,
# `getStaticPaths` emits only pages in those locales. Skip for a
# full-locale build of the website.
# WEBSITE_BUILD_LOCALES=fr,en

# Optional surgical filter — comma-separated `locale/path` keys.
# Entries ending in `/` target the locale landing (e.g. `fr/`).
# Astro wipes `dist/` on each build; deploy via `rclone copy`
# (overlay, never deletes existing files at the edge).
# WEBSITE_BUILD_PATHS=fr/colisee,en/colosseum,fr/
